<title>USA: Apogee Inc Q1 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Apogee Inc Q1 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>KING OF PRUSSIA, Pa. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net revenues				     $19,200     $19,668</p>
<p> Gross profit					 3,703	 4,677</p>
<p> Selling and administrative expenses	  3,277	 3,573</p>
<p>Amortization of excess of cost over</p>
<p>  net assets required				 539	   576</p>
<p> (Loss) income from operations		 ( 113)	   528</p>
<p> Net (loss) income				 ( 420)	   348</p>
<p> Net (loss) income per common share	 ( 0.04)	  0.04</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding    9,915,806   9,881,722</p>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except share and per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Apogee Inc attributed the loss to a previously announced restructuring, under which it plans to terminate long-term care operations and selected group practices.</p>
<p>The company said that excluding the losses from the restructuring, it broke even in the first quarter.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
